From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yu Wei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:10:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Lay out tabs at tab stops

A preserved tab kept the advance it was shaped with: a space's in fonts
that map U+0009, the .notdef box's in the rest. StyleProperty::TabStops
(TabStops: the distance between tab stops and the least a tab advances,
None by default, which leaves a tab its shaped advance) lets the
embedder give them, as CSS tab-size counts them in the block
container's space, which parley doesn't know.

The line breaker gives a tab the advance to the next tab stop from
where it is on its line (past the floats beside it, line_x, and the
indent), or to the one after it when that is nearer than the least
advance, and takes the run again from the tab
(ShapedText::set_cluster_advance). With no tab stops (an interval of 0)
a tab has only its letter spacing (Blink's Font::TabWidth). The
min/max-content measurer works the advance out on each of its two
lines.

The shaper shapes a tab as a space, so that it draws nothing.
